# Data cache — publish the small per-symbol CSVs at local_data root;
# deny ALL subdirectories by default (Kraken_batch 32G, Kraken_funding_rates 436M,
# holdout_sealed 1.9G sealed). Deny-by-default, not name enumeration: a new bulk
# directory added later is caught automatically.
trading-bot/local_data/*/
# Belt-and-braces: the single-use holdout must never become publishable
**/holdout_sealed/
# Exceeds GitHub's 100MB per-file hard limit — would reject the push
trading-bot/local_data/BTCUSDT_1m.csv

# HOLDOUT-CARRYING CACHE FILES — excluded from publication (2026-07-26).
# Each file below was measured today to contain rows inside the frozen
# holdout_range 2026-01-01..2026-06-30 (campaign_data_policy.yaml:18). The
# subdirectory deny-by-default rule above does not reach them: they are loose
# files at local_data/ root, in the default un-prefixed Binance cache slot that
# every CcxtFetcher/FundingRateFetcher consumer reads.
#
# This block IS a name enumeration, and that is a known weakness — the same
# weakness the comment above rejects for subdirectories. It is used here because
# the property being guarded is a DATE RANGE INSIDE file contents, which
# .gitignore cannot express at all: no pattern can ask "does this CSV have a row
# after 2026-01-01". The enumeration is therefore a stopgap over a set measured
# on 2026-07-26, not a rule that catches the next contaminated file. A new cache
# file crossing into the holdout range will NOT be caught here, and no range check
# exists anywhere today that would catch it — that gap is open, not closed
# (tasks/lessons.md L-2026-07-26-A).
trading-bot/local_data/BTCUSDT_1h.csv
trading-bot/local_data/ETHUSDT_1h.csv
trading-bot/local_data/BTCUSDT_1d.csv
trading-bot/local_data/ETHUSDT_1d.csv
trading-bot/local_data/fear_greed_daily.csv
trading-bot/local_data/BTCUSDT_funding_8h.csv
trading-bot/local_data/ETHUSDT_funding_8h.csv

